section.prose:
The status lifecycle reuses the component vocabulary's five spellings verbatim rather than inventing a research-specific enum (
): a proposal under review authors as design-pass , its human status phrase carried in the banner. The class design borrows the Lean reference-manual patterns the component corpus already adopted — titled boxes, stable anchors, status attributes, checked-shape examples
.

list.item:
O2
— whether the per-crate lean tier should get an XML class at all. It is off the corpus main-path by design and is prose with almost no cross-references, coined anchors, or citations — the thin parse-is-validate value (dated-section shape, status presence) may not repay the ceremony. Options: (a) ship the minimal
crate-status
class as designed; (b) keep the lean tier in Markdown indefinitely and cut over only research and workflow; (c) fold CHANGELOG into STATUS and let beads plus git history carry the dated record (

). Recommendation: (c) for CHANGELOG, (a) for STATUS.

section.prose:
The research-record class survived authoring its own design record. Every feature the charter names was exercised by this file: the status banner, nested sections, tables (the substrate and the inventory below), a code listing, coined-label anchors (
,
,
,
) with intra-document resolution, and a register-key citation (
). The class vocabulary was sufficient; no fallback to Markdown was needed, and the bootstrap validates clean under check-docs .
